        <item>
            <title>0.12.5</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 22:42:41 +0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.12.5</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.12.5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.12.5</h2>
<ul>
<li>Four-finger tap, rebuilt on the trackpad&#x27;s own sensor states: a palm resting on the pad with a three-finger tap or drag can never open the Compass any more, while real four-finger taps (including beside a resting palm, or landing four and clicking later) fire reliably; taps right after the Mac wakes no longer misfire</li>
<li>Press W / A / S / D while any menu is open to jump straight to that Compass menu (e.g. A in the universal menu opens the app launcher); if your navigation keys are set to WASD they keep navigating</li>
<li>A folder&#x27;s ring of pills now matches the main ring&#x27;s size exactly</li>
<li>Pills inside a folder never stick to or merge with a close neighbour any more — at rest, while hovering, and while the folder opens</li>
<li>Inside a folder, the strand now meets each pill centred on the side facing the folder — no more off-centre attachment in rearranged folders</li>
<li>Hovering any pill now swells the whole pill — body and icon together, the same motion as a folder charging</li>
<li>Firing a pill no longer bounces it — the pill holds still and the ring pulse is the confirmation</li>
<li>An open folder tilts as a whole toward your pointer again, and while a folder is open the menu&#x27;s centre stays put — only the folder follows your hand; a Confirm/Cancel pair keeps the centre on your cursor</li>
<li>The hub bounces softly when a menu swap lands, and its glyph changes in a clean cut</li>
<li>The goo strand now meets coloured pills exactly like black ones, keeps a clean neck through the ⌥ flip instead of jittering, and flows off the hub&#x27;s edge like off a folder pill</li>
<li>Faster and steadier: the first open after a long idle no longer stutters, and switching menus in the Compass keeps the pills alive instead of rebuilding them (the swap-glide hitch is gone)</li>
<li>Settings side panel: the cards wear the same clean glass as the pill library, tuned to stay colour-true</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
